{
  "note": "🖊️ The text-control keyboard law every renderer shares (ticket 26/09/30 design §22.7), the text counterpart of the number-control keyboard law: for a text field that holds a draft (`commit: \"blur\"`), what a key does given the field's kind and the modifiers held (`primary` is Ctrl, ⌘ on macOS). `action` is `newline` (the field inserts a line break, nothing is dispatched), `commit` (the draft is dispatched without waiting for focus to leave), `revert` (the draft is dropped and the published value shown again) or null (the key is not the field's). Escape reverts; a single-line field commits on Enter; a multi-line field (`longText`) inserts a line on Enter, with or without Shift, and commits on Ctrl/⌘+Enter; a single-line Shift+Enter and every Alt chord are not the field's (Alt+Enter is a shell chord). Rust `text_input_key`, TypeScript `uiTextInputKey`.",
